      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name} This is expected behaviour, as gravity is no longer a force.  We have some dev notes coming out here soon that will give a more detailed explanation.  Here is a snippet from that info.\n\n\"Previously: Gravity acted as a force which competed with Pull.  To get a specific look you needed to balance the ratio of these two values.\n\nNow: Gravity acts directly as that ratio of how much gravity deforms the rest position of your bones.  A value of one means your bones will always fall straight down, a value of 0.5 means it will hover half way between the rest position and the world down vector.\n\nIn practice we have found this to be easier to tweak the look you are going for.\n\nSince gravity is no longer a force, Pull is the only force that dictates how fast the bones will fall into their new rest position.  Previously many things that pointed straight down would look like (Pull: 0 Gravity: 0.3).  Now that would need to be configured like (Pull: 0.3 Gravity: 1.0).\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
