  "details": "# Issue: \n\nWith Phys Bones Version 1.1 Gravity was changed to only apply at resting position according to the change log. This works fine in most scenarios, but when you don't have any pull on a Phys Bone, Gravity just does nothing. This results in the bone just being static at what ever position your movement or someone grabbing it moved it to.\n\n**Reproduction Steps:**\n\n1. Create a bone chain in Unity made out of 3 elements.  \n\n2. Apply the Phys Bone settings as shown in the Attachments (you can ignore the Max Angle Curve)  \n\nIf you do this you will notice that even if you move the Phys Bone away from their origin by either spinning it around or by grabbing it, Gravity will not have an affect on it and it will not be pulled down.\n\n# Expected Behavior:\n\nIf there is no Pull to bring a bone back into it's resting position (so Pull being at 0), Gravity should just always be applied.\n\nOther than that I have to say that I don't think changing the way Gravity behaves in general is a good decision. It made sense with how it worked before (it would always be applied as a force no matter what) since... well... that's how gravity works. Because if something has pull on it, I would expect gravity to try and fight against that pull. (depending on the orientation obviously)\n\nI do think that the change Stiffness received makes though as the new behavior is closer to (at least in my opinion) how you expect it to work.\n\n# Attachments:\n\nHere is a video showcasing the issue:\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/19uvty.mp4\n\nHere is a picture of the used Phys Bone settings:",
